<DocsLayout title="Install Haft v9" description="The short installation path for the current Haft v9 release.">
  <h1>Install Haft v9</h1>

  <pre><code>curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/m0n0x41d/haft/main/install.sh | bash

cd /path/to/project
haft init --claude   # or: haft init --codex
# fully restart the coding agent</code></pre>

  <p>
    The current release is
    <a href="https://github.com/m0n0x41d/haft/releases/tag/v9.0.2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">v9.0.2</a>.
    The v9 archive contains the Haft CLI and no Open-Sleigh, ERTS, Elixir, or
    BEAM runtime.
  </p>

  <h2>Upgrade safety</h2>

  <ol>
    <li>Stop every host process that can run <code>haft serve</code>.</li>
    <li>Back up the project <code>.haft/</code> directory and its global project ledger.</li>
    <li>Install v9.0.2 and record <code>haft version</code>.</li>
    <li>Re-run init for only the host targets you use, then fully restart them.</li>
  </ol>

  <p>
    A successful v9 installer removes only the managed legacy path
    <code>~/.haft/runtimes/open-sleigh/current</code>. It preserves all
    <code>~/.open-sleigh/</code> data and the independent
    <code>~/.haft/runtimes/haft-embed/</code> tree.
  </p>

  <h2>Removed command migration</h2>

  <p>
    Replace <code>haft run</code> and <code>haft harness</code> automation with
    direct host-agent work or a separately operated runner. Haft can still keep
    runner-neutral commission and run records, but it no longer executes the
    coding work itself.
  </p>

  <p><a href="/docs/install">Read the complete install, verification, and upgrade notes</a>.</p>
</DocsLayout>
